name 'designing-reliable-apps-postassessment-q15_2025'

question 'A developer is deciding whether to store a user\'s workout history as local data or as live data on a remote server. Which tradeoff statement about local data is most accurate?'

wrong 'Local data is always the right choice because it loads instantly and never requires a network request'
right 'Local data loads faster and works offline, but it can be lost if the user switches devices or clears the app'
wrong 'Local data is more secure than live data because it is never transmitted over a network'
wrong 'Local data is only appropriate for apps that do not need to display personalized information'

allow_multiple_attempts true

